{"id":"u55","kelas":"kerja","no":8,"judul":"Laporan dan Data","title":"Reports and Data","emoji":"📈","ringkas":"Angka, persen, tren naik-turun, dan membaca grafik","ready":true,"goals":["membaca dan menyebut **angka besar**, desimal, pecahan, dan persen dalam bahasa Inggris","menjelaskan **tren** naik, turun, dan stabil: [[rise]], [[fall]], [[remain stable]], [[fluctuate]]","memakai kata keterangan **tingkat perubahan**: [[sharply]], [[steadily]], [[slightly]], [[dramatically]]","memakai preposisi pada data: [[from ... to ...]], [[by ...]], [[at ...]], [[to reach ...]]","menjelaskan **grafik** (bar chart, line graph, pie chart) dan membandingkan data","menulis ringkasan laporan data yang singkat dan akurat"],"lesson":[{"t":"intro","text":"Laporan kerja hampir selalu memuat **angka**: penjualan, biaya, jumlah pelanggan, dan target. Kamu perlu bisa **menyebut angka dengan benar** dan **menjelaskan perubahannya** dengan kata yang tepat. Semua angka dalam contoh unit ini hanya data rekaan untuk latihan."},{"t":"grammar","title":"1. Menyebut angka","table":[["Angka","Cara menyebut"],["1,250","[[one thousand, two hundred and fifty]]"],["15,000","[[fifteen thousand]]"],["2,500,000","[[two point five million]] atau [[two million, five hundred thousand]]"],["0.5","[[zero point five]] / [[point five]]"],["3.75","[[three point seven five]]"],["1/2, 1/4, 3/4","[[a half]], [[a quarter]], [[three quarters]]"],["25%","[[twenty-five percent]]"],["Rp 500,000","[[five hundred thousand rupiah]]"]]},{"t":"warn","title":"Hundred, thousand, million tanpa -s","text":"Setelah angka, [[hundred]], [[thousand]], dan [[million]] **tidak memakai -s**: [[three hundred]], [[five thousand]], [[two million]]. Pakai -s hanya tanpa angka: [[hundreds of people]], [[thousands of customers]]."},{"t":"grammar","title":"2. Kata kerja dan kata benda untuk tren","table":[["Arah","Kata kerja","Kata benda"],["**Naik**","[[rise]], [[increase]], [[grow]], [[go up]], [[climb]]","[[a rise]], [[an increase]], [[growth]]"],["**Turun**","[[fall]], [[decrease]], [[drop]], [[decline]], [[go down]]","[[a fall]], [[a decrease]], [[a drop]], [[a decline]]"],["**Stabil**","[[remain stable]], [[stay the same]], [[level off]]","[[a plateau]]"],["**Naik-turun**","[[fluctuate]]","[[a fluctuation]]"],["**Puncak / terendah**","[[peak at ...]] / [[hit a low of ...]]","[[a peak]] / [[a low]]"]]},{"t":"grammar","title":"3. Kata keterangan tingkat perubahan","table":[["Perubahan besar / cepat","Perubahan kecil / lambat"],["[[sharply]], [[dramatically]], [[significantly]], [[rapidly]]","[[slightly]], [[gradually]], [[steadily]], [[slowly]]"],["[[Sales rose sharply.]]","[[Sales rose slightly.]]"],["[[a sharp rise]]","[[a slight rise]]"]]},{"t":"tip","title":"Dua pola kalimat yang setara","text":"Kata kerja + keterangan: [[Sales **rose sharply**.]] Kata benda + sifat: [[There was **a sharp rise** in sales.]] Kedua kalimat bermakna sama. Pakai bergantian agar laporan tidak monoton."},{"t":"grammar","title":"4. Preposisi pada data","table":[["Preposisi","Fungsi","Contoh"],["**from ... to ...**","nilai awal ke akhir","[[Sales rose from 200 to 250.]]"],["**by**","besar perubahan","[[Sales rose by 50 units.]] / [[by 25%]]"],["**to**","nilai akhir","[[Costs fell to 80.]]"],["**at**","nilai pada puncak/stabil","[[Sales peaked at 300.]] / [[It remained at 120.]]"],["**of**","angka dalam kata benda","[[an increase of 10%]]"],["**in**","hal yang berubah","[[a rise in sales]]"],["**between ... and ...**","rentang waktu","[[between January and June]]"]]},{"t":"vocab","title":"5. Kosakata penting","items":[{"en":"figure","id":"angka / data","ex":"The figures are accurate."},{"en":"percentage","id":"persentase","ex":"What percentage is that?"},{"en":"proportion","id":"proporsi","ex":"A large proportion bought online."},{"en":"majority / minority","id":"mayoritas / minoritas","ex":"The majority prefers online shopping."},{"en":"average","id":"rata-rata","ex":"The average is 45."},{"en":"total","id":"total","ex":"The total is 1,000."},{"en":"revenue","id":"pendapatan","ex":"Revenue increased this year."},{"en":"profit / loss","id":"laba / rugi","ex":"The company made a profit."},{"en":"expenses","id":"pengeluaran","ex":"Expenses fell by 5%."},{"en":"target","id":"target","ex":"We reached the target."},{"en":"trend","id":"tren","ex":"The trend is upward."},{"en":"compared with","id":"dibandingkan dengan","ex":"Sales rose compared with last year."},{"en":"account for","id":"menyumbang / mewakili","ex":"Women account for 40% of staff."},{"en":"chart / graph","id":"bagan / grafik","ex":"The chart shows monthly sales."},{"en":"axis","id":"sumbu","ex":"The horizontal axis shows months."}]},{"t":"grammar","title":"6. Menjelaskan grafik","table":[["Fungsi","Ungkapan"],["Membuka","[[This chart shows ...]] / [[The graph illustrates ...]]"],["Menyebut tren","[[Sales rose steadily from January to June.]]"],["Membandingkan","[[Product A sold more than Product B.]] / [[Compared with 2024, ...]]"],["Pecahan pie chart","[[Marketing accounts for 20% of the budget.]]"],["Menyimpulkan","[[Overall, the trend is upward.]] / [[In conclusion, ...]]"]]},{"t":"dialog","title":"Teks 1: Ringkasan penjualan (data rekaan)","lines":[{"who":"Report","en":"This chart shows monthly sales of a small shop from January to June.","id":"Grafik ini menunjukkan penjualan bulanan sebuah toko kecil dari Januari sampai Juni."},{"who":"Report","en":"Sales rose steadily from 200 units in January to 300 units in April. After that, they dropped slightly to 280 in May.","id":"Penjualan naik stabil dari 200 unit pada Januari menjadi 300 unit pada April. Setelah itu turun sedikit menjadi 280 pada Mei."},{"who":"Report","en":"In June, sales climbed sharply and reached a peak of 350 units, which is an increase of 75% compared with January.","id":"Pada Juni, penjualan melonjak tajam dan mencapai puncak 350 unit, yaitu kenaikan 75% dibandingkan Januari."},{"who":"Report","en":"Overall, the trend is upward.","id":"Secara keseluruhan, trennya naik."}]},{"t":"dialog","title":"Dialog: Membahas grafik","lines":[{"who":"Mr. Adi","en":"Dina, can you explain this chart for us?","id":"Dina, bisakah kamu menjelaskan grafik ini kepada kami?"},{"who":"Dina","en":"Of course. Revenue rose from 400 million rupiah to 500 million between January and June.","id":"Tentu. Pendapatan naik dari 400 juta rupiah menjadi 500 juta antara Januari dan Juni."},{"who":"Mr. Adi","en":"So that's an increase of how much?","id":"Jadi kenaikannya berapa?"},{"who":"Dina","en":"It is an increase of 100 million rupiah, or 25 percent.","id":"Kenaikan 100 juta rupiah, atau 25 persen."},{"who":"Mr. Adi","en":"Good. And what about expenses?","id":"Bagus. Bagaimana dengan pengeluaran?"},{"who":"Dina","en":"Expenses remained stable at around 300 million.","id":"Pengeluaran stabil di sekitar 300 juta."}]},{"t":"summary","items":["Angka: [[hundred]], [[thousand]], [[million]] tanpa -s setelah angka; desimal dengan [[point]].","Tren: [[rise]], [[fall]], [[remain stable]], [[fluctuate]], [[peak at]].","Tingkat: [[sharply]], [[dramatically]] (besar); [[slightly]], [[gradually]] (kecil).","Preposisi: [[from ... to ...]], [[by ...]], [[at ...]], [[an increase of ...]].","Menjelaskan grafik: [[This chart shows ...]], akhiri dengan [[Overall, ...]]."]}],"practice":[{"type":"match","q":"Pasangkan kosakata dengan artinya:","pairs":[["revenue","pendapatan"],["expenses","pengeluaran"],["profit","laba"],["average","rata-rata"],["trend","tren"]],"exp":"Kosakata data.","k":"5b4e3f2d"},{"type":"match","q":"Pasangkan angka dengan cara menyebutnya:","pairs":[["15,000","fifteen thousand"],["0.5","zero point five"],["25%","twenty-five percent"],["3/4","three quarters"]],"exp":"Menyebut angka.","k":"063cc078"},{"type":"match","q":"Pasangkan kata kerja dengan arah tren:","pairs":[["rise","naik"],["drop","turun"],["remain stable","stabil"],["fluctuate","naik-turun"]],"exp":"Arah tren.","k":"e49fd00d"},{"type":"mcq","q":"1,250 dibaca...","options":["one thousand, two hundred and fifty","one thousands two hundreds fifty","twelve fifty thousand","one two five oh"],"answer":0,"exp":"Tanpa -s.","k":"e4def557"},{"type":"mcq","q":"Yang benar adalah...","options":["three hundred","three hundreds","three of hundred","three hundred's"],"answer":0,"exp":"hundred tanpa -s setelah angka.","k":"38a0863e"},{"type":"mcq","q":"Yang benar adalah...","options":["thousands of people","thousand of people","thousands people","thousand people of"],"answer":0,"exp":"Tanpa angka: thousands of.","k":"8f49d27c"},{"type":"mcq","q":"Kata keterangan untuk perubahan kecil adalah...","options":["slightly","sharply","dramatically","rapidly"],"answer":0,"exp":"slightly = sedikit.","k":"07081359"},{"type":"mcq","q":"Kata keterangan untuk perubahan besar adalah...","options":["sharply","slightly","gradually","slowly"],"answer":0,"exp":"sharply = tajam.","k":"48408d08"},{"type":"mcq","q":"\"Sales rose from 200 to 250.\" Kenaikannya adalah...","options":["50 unit atau 25%","25 unit atau 50%","250 unit","20%"],"answer":0,"exp":"250 - 200 = 50; 50/200 = 25%.","k":"d69ef544"},{"type":"mcq","q":"\"Costs fell by 10%.\" Artinya biaya...","options":["turun sebesar 10%","naik 10%","menjadi 10%","stabil di 10%"],"answer":0,"exp":"by = besar perubahan.","k":"aaee6624"},{"type":"mcq","q":"\"Sales peaked at 300.\" Artinya...","options":["penjualan mencapai puncak 300","penjualan mulai 300","penjualan turun 300","penjualan stabil"],"answer":0,"exp":"peaked at.","k":"750212e4"},{"type":"mcq","q":"Kalimat yang benar adalah...","options":["There was a sharp rise in sales.","There was a sharp rises in sales.","There were a sharp rise in sales.","There was sharply rise in sales."],"answer":0,"exp":"a + adjective + noun.","k":"58fd60da"},{"type":"mcq","q":"Kalimat yang benar adalah...","options":["Sales increased steadily.","Sales increased steady.","Sales increase steadily yesterday.","Sales steadily increased of."],"answer":0,"exp":"Kata kerja + adverb.","k":"7e14533